       "This specification defines how Gravity compiles agentic programs into durable\nworkflow graphs. Agent workflows combine deterministic code, model calls, tool\ncalls, memory access, human-review decisions, retries, compensation, and final outputs.\nBecause these workflows contain nondeterminism, replay boundaries are part of\nthe semantics rather than an implementation detail.\n",
       :source-file-sha256
       "cd418638f117af98501032681cbbfa7b5a9c74991c44fdfa129d0c63b81388bc",
       :id "facet/ai-build-tools/a6/331-706",
       :kind :normative-context,
       :document-id "A6",
       :end-byte 706,
